From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:47:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 384/384] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: scan the
 keyboard on interrupts

EINT10 now delivers the AW9523 interrupt. With the expander's interrupt
thread serialized, row interrupt scans read the right keys. Switch the
station keyboard from 20 ms polling to row interrupts. Keep scanning
every 20 ms while a key is held, so that same-row combinations such as
Left Shift+Z and Ctrl+Alt are seen.

The experiment-only matrix_keypad.poll_override can still return a
running station to polling.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts      | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 1e3d607c6..52aa9ef07 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -208,6 +208,15 @@ &aw9523 {
 	#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * Scan the keyboard on row interrupts, and poll only while a key is held,
+ * so that a second key in an already asserted row is still seen.
+ */
+&{/keyboard-matrix} {
+	/delete-property/ poll-interval;
+	held-poll-interval = <20>;
+};
+
 &thermal {
 	mediatek,toprgu = <&watchdog>;
 	mediatek,hw-reset-millicelsius = <117000>;
